A missing file argument is reported on stderr as `File … does not exist` and makes the exit code 1, while the existing file after it is still outlined.
== args
input/missing.ts
input/existing.ts
== file input/existing.ts
// This file exists
== stdout
input/existing.ts (1 line)
This file exists
== stderr
File input/missing.ts does not exist
== exit 1
